Project goal is analyze the relationship between population, income group, and GDP by region and country since 1960.
Was Performed:
Hierarchical analysis (Treemap): Visual distribution of population by region and country (from China and India to small states). 
Economic cross-section: Comparison of average GDP depending on a country's affiliation with a specific economic zone (income group). 
Interactivity: Filtering by year has been added to track changes over time.

The project included:
Data Preparation: Cleaning and transforming source data using Power Query (handling empty values, changing data types). 
Creating relationships between tables of regions, countries, and metrics.
Using treemaps to display population structure and bar charts to compare economic indicators. Slice synchronization was configured for easy navigation by year.
